        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: सम्यक्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सम्यक् (samyak) — \"rightly, properly, exactly so\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सम्यक् (samyak) confirms that a thing has been done right."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is sam, \"together\" — the sam- inside समुद्रः and संस्कृतम् — joined to a piece meaning \"turned, directed\": turned the right way, all of a piece. Beside साधु it is the cooler of the two. साधु praises the person; सम्यक् (samyak) confirms the thing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five short replies, and the difference between praising and confirming."
            }
          ]
        },
